  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "• Add proper CancellationToken handling in Converter.ExecuteOnWorkerAsync\n• Cancel cleanly while waiting for an available worker (no forced kill)\n• Kill the active worker via WorkerHandle.Kill() when cancellation occurs during processing\n• Keep worker pool consistent after kill/removal and allow new workers to be spawned for subsequent requests\n• Preserve timeout behavior and existing conversion error handling",
